# GridDungeon editor menu (`MenuItem`)

Authority: `GridDungeonEditorMenus` (Editor) + `GridDungeonEditorMenuHints` (runtime log copy) in **griddungeon-game**.

## GridDungeon menu = Edit Mode / authoring

| OK on `GridDungeon/` menu | Not OK |
|---|---|
| Open editor windows (Floor Editor, Dev Tools, Save Editor, Dev Tools Map) | Play Mode **actions** (combat, fill party, flee, hub jump, …) |
| Create/regenerate assets, scenes, prefabs, catalogs | `[MenuItem(..., true)]` gated on `Application.isPlaying` |
| Content ensure / compact / sync pipelines | Duplicate of a button inside **Tools → Dev Tools** |

Opening **Dev Tools** / **Dev Tools Map** / **Save Editor** from the menu is OK — opens a **window**; Play Mode work happens inside it.

## Play Mode dev actions

- **Tools → Dev Tools** — buttons + live status (authoritative UI).
- **F-keys** — `GamePhaseDevShortcuts` in Play Mode.
- **Save Editor** — save file + campaign flags (Edit Mode write; F5/F8 mirrors in Play Mode).

No `GridDungeon/Dev/` or `Tools/Play Mode/` menu commands for phase/combat/party shortcuts.

## Nested submenu layout

| Top-level | Submenus / items |
|---|---|
| **Tools** | Dev Tools, Dev Tools Map, Save Editor, Log MVP1 Save Path |
| **Scenes** | Create Dev Bootstrap, Create Play Mode Exploration Scene |
| **Content** | Floor Editor, Ensure MVP1 ContentDatabase, Ensure MVP1 S1 Story Events, Ensure Campaign Flag Registry, Compact floor list, **Floor Connector/** |
| **Floor Art** | **Preview/**, **Templates/**, **Lighting/**, **Dev Prefabs/**, Sync S1 Stratum Defaults |
| **Map** | Create catalog, Wire SVG textures |
| **Hub** | Cinemachine brain, Greybox town prefab |
| **Floor Transition** | Create stairs beat prefab, Sync catalog |

`Create → GridDungeon → …` (`CreateAssetMenu`) is a separate Unity menu — do not conflate with top-bar `GridDungeon/`.

## PR / agent checklist

- [ ] New `[MenuItem]` is Edit Mode / authoring — not a Play Mode action dupe of Dev Tools
- [ ] Path added to `GridDungeonEditorMenuHints` + `GridDungeonEditorMenus`; logs/docs use `Display()` or `*Display` readonly fields
- [ ] README / design-docs menu copy updated when paths change
